From 80f7470ccc393bec90b3f427662eb55192a5237e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anders Jensen-Waud <5827908+ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 19:55:49 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] ricursive: TP=2 over two GB10s, full layers to 1M
 context, decode-row graphs

Rank 0 drives, rank 1 follows: a plan word (op, rows, p0, head rows, ids) is gathered before each call. Each
layer's o_proj and down_proj fp32 partials are all-gathered (tp_group: NCCL, or RoCE writes with
TF_RICURSIVE_ROCE=1) and added once in rank order (tf_ripple_rank_sum) before the post-norms; the head's vocab
halves are gathered. admit(121, 1 | 2); weightShare: the cut share plus the whole bf16 embedding.

Full (NoPE) layers leave window_attention's decode rows (refused above 4,096 keys): decode rows on main's
tree_attention (512-key groups, merged in order) over a 16-bit (bf16, unquantised) cache of context + 128 rows; prompt
chunks on window_attention's head dim 128 prompt rows with q padded from 10 to 12 heads a key head
(tf_ripple_heads). TF_RICURSIVE_FULL_PROMPT=0 keeps prompt chunks on tree rows (prompt == decode bits).
Decode rows replay as CUDA graphs keyed by 64-group buckets (TF_RICURSIVE_GRAPHS=1, bit-identical to eager).
tf-ricursive gains follow, long and bench modes.
